# Secret group `side-role`: The `semprec_side` role password and connection string.
# Loaded by: semprec-ai-gateway.service, semprec-restore-test.service.
#
# Ownership and mode are load-bearing: `root:root 0600`. systemd reads EnvironmentFile= as root
# before dropping privileges. provision.sh installs this template to
# /opt/semprec/shared/env/side-role.env only when that file does not exist, so an operator's values are
# never overwritten by a rerun, and it never prints a value. A key belongs to exactly one group
# (docs/adr/2026-10-03-per-service-secret-groups.md); this file is excluded from restic backups.

# SEMPREC_SIDE_DB_PASSWORD: the password the operator sets with
# `ALTER ROLE semprec_side WITH PASSWORD '...'` (migration 0040_least_privilege_roles.sql creates
# the role itself, with no password until this is done). Distinct from SEMPREC_DATA_DB_PASSWORD in
# data-role.env, so the two roles are never accidentally given the same password. Used, together
# with POSTGRES_DB in postgres.env, to build the connection string below.
SEMPREC_SIDE_DB_PASSWORD=

# SEMPREC_SIDE_DATABASE_URL: shared by every `semprec_side`-role process (semprec-ai-gateway and
# the restore test, per docs/operations/database-roles.md) — none of them ever writes a
# choke-point table, so one read-only-on-choke-point, full-on-side-tables role covers all of
# them. Built from
# SEMPREC_SIDE_DB_PASSWORD above, e.g.:
# postgres://semprec_side:<SEMPREC_SIDE_DB_PASSWORD>@127.0.0.1:5432/semprec
SEMPREC_SIDE_DATABASE_URL=
